<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Albulena</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1457">1457</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Battle of Ujëbardha</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Albulena was fought on 2 September 1457 in central Albania, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skanderbeg">Skanderbeg</a> defeated a large Ottoman army under Isa Bey Evrenos. Skanderbeg had withdrawn into the mountains, letting the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> spread out to plunder, before attacking their camp by surprise. The victory was among his greatest and brought him praise across Christian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-albulena.jpg" alt="Battle of Albulena" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dhimitër Frëngu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Assault_on_Turkish_encampment.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
